{"repositoryId":402492488,"availability":"available","full":"jameskerr/react-arborist","name":"react-arborist","description":"The complete tree view component for React","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":3712,"forks":187,"created":"2021-09-02T16:37:55Z","updated":"2026-10-11T00:54:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["arborist","react","tree","treeview","treeview-component"],"demo":"https://codesandbox.io/s/the-simplest-tree-7tbedw","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T06:18:50.263Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T06:18:50.263Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T06:18:50.263Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:33:15.235Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"curated-list","name":"Awesome React Components","url":"https://github.com/brillout/awesome-react-components"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:33:15.235Z","stars":3710,"forks":187},{"at":"2026-10-19T06:18:50.263Z","stars":3712,"forks":187}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The tree view is ubiquitous in software applications. This library provides the React ecosystem with a complete solution to build the equivalent of a VSCode sidebar, Mac Finder, Windows Explorer, or Sketch/Figma layers panel.","Here is a Gmail sidebar clone built with react-arborist.","From react-arborist v4, react-dnd and react-dnd-html5-backend are peer dependencies rather than bundled dependencies. This matters because react-dnd registers a global singleton (globalThis[Symbol.for('REACTDNDCONTEXTINSTANCE')]). If your application and react-arborist each bundled their own copy, you would end up with two independent singletons, causing drag-and-drop to silently break or throw \"Cannot have two HTML5 backends at the same time\"."],"features":["Drag and drop sorting","Virtualized rendering","Selection synchronization","Callbacks (onScroll, onActivate, onSelect)","Controlled or uncontrolled trees"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jameskerr/re